- env var SHELL

- PROG["sh"] \\
  If awk_stat determines that /bin/sh (or whatever the administrator
  puts in the _progs[]) exists, this will be the ``safe'' shell that m2
  uses for internal work.  The key to the PROG array is the basename of
  the executable.  If the administrator chooses, she may remove sh from
  the list; in this case PROG["sh"] will not exist as an element.

- uuPROGuu["sh"] \\
  This is an m2 Array which is a copy of the Awk PROG[] array.  Visible
  to the user, but not modifiable.  Used by build_prog_cmdline().  "sh"
  may or may not exist depending on PROG[].
  

EXISTING FUNCTIONS:
- exec_prog_cmdline(ELEM, PATH) \\
  Call build_prog_cmdline to construct a command line, then execute it
  with Awk's system() function.  Stdout and stderr are always both
  redirected to /dev/null when this function is used (MODE_IO_SILENT).

- default_shell() \\
  Return a path to "the shell".  (About to be split into two functions.)
  1. Symbol "M2_SHELL", if defined
  2. Env var "SHELL", if defined
  3. PROG["sh"], if defined
  4. Error!


